 "result_text": "`Chain.from_json(chain.to_json())` now works for chains that contain predicates. I ran a smaller version of your example (one `is_in` on `edge_match`) and the JSON round-trips unchanged. I didn't run the repo's test suite.\n\nWhen loading `filter_dict`/`edge_match` values, `maybe_filter_dict_from_json` in `graphistry/compute/ast.py` called `ASTPredicate.from_json`, the base-class loader. That loader tries to build the abstract base class instead of the `IsIn`, `GT`, etc. named in the JSON. I pointed it at the existing type-dispatching loader in `graphistry/compute/predicates/from_json.py` and added the import. This applies to every predicate type in that registry, not just `is_in`.",
